  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:6$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($4$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($6$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $2,$ we divide the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4÷2}{6÷2}=\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $18,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of the previous fraction by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\times 6}{3\\times 6} & =\\frac{12}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $6$ |\n| $12$ | $18$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
